<figure class="ops-figure ops-lock" data-ops-lock aria-labelledby="ops-lock-title">
  <div class="ops-figure-title" id="ops-lock-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Which action releases the reader?</div>
  <p class="ops-small">Illustrative lock-only schedule · H and W are session labels, not process IDs</p>
  <div class="ops-lock-scene" data-live>
    <div class="ops-card"><b>Holder H</b><strong data-holder>Idle in transaction</strong><span data-holder-detail>LOCK statement finished; transaction open</span></div>
    <div class="ops-dependency"><div class="ops-link"><span data-edge>H holds</span><span class="ops-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><div class="ops-card"><b>orders</b><strong data-lock>ACCESS EXCLUSIVE held</strong><span data-lock-detail>Conflicts with W’s ACCESS SHARE request</span></div><div class="ops-link"><span class="ops-arrow ops-reader-arrow" aria-hidden="true">←</span><span data-reader-edge>W needs</span></div></div>
    <div class="ops-card"><b>History W</b><strong data-waiter>Active · Lock / relation</strong><span data-waiter-detail>SELECT has not returned rows</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="ops-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">H acquired the table lock inside BEGIN. The lock command returned, but H did not end the transaction. W is waiting to read orders.</p>
  <div class="ops-controls">
    <div class="ops-choice"><label for="ops-intervention">Intervention</label><select id="ops-intervention" data-action><option value="rollback">Owner rolls back H</option><option value="cancel-holder">Cancel H’s query</option><option value="cancel-waiter">Cancel W’s query</option><option value="terminate">Terminate H’s session</option></select></div>
    <div class="ops-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 playback">
      <button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span>
    </div><div class="ops-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Each choice starts again at the same wait. The model assumes H has changed no rows. Cancellation, transaction end and session termination have different scopes; none is a substitute for checking the client’s outcome.</figcaption>
  <details><summary>All outcomes, as text</summary><ul><li>Owner rollback: H ends its transaction and releases the lock. W can read 103 then 101; the application still has to consume the result and return its client.</li><li>Cancel H: there is no running query to cancel. H’s open transaction can keep the table lock, so W remains blocked.</li><li>Cancel W: W’s statement ends with an error; H keeps the table lock. In an explicit transaction, W must roll back before reuse. Returning that client does not repair the blocker.</li><li>Terminate H: H’s session ends and its unfinished transaction aborts. The lock is released and W can read. H’s client connection is lost and must be discarded.</li></ul></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-ops-lock]').forEach(root => {
    const choose = root.querySelector('[data-action]');
    const base = ['Idle in transaction','LOCK statement finished; transaction open','ACCESS EXCLUSIVE held','Conflicts with W’s ACCESS SHARE request','Active · Lock / relation','SELECT has not returned rows','H holds','W needs'];
    const fields = ['holder','holder-detail','lock','lock-detail','waiter','waiter-detail','edge','reader-edge'];
    const stories = {
      rollback: [
        'H acquired the table lock inside BEGIN. The lock command returned, but H did not end the transaction. W is waiting to read orders.',
        'H’s owner sends ROLLBACK on H’s own connection. Sending the command is not yet evidence that the transaction ended.',
        'ROLLBACK completes. H no longer holds the table lock, and W’s read can acquire its required lock and finish.',
        'W returns 103 then 101. The application consumes the result and returns W’s client; check queued and new requests as well.'
      ],
      'cancel-holder': [
        'H’s LOCK command has finished. Its open transaction, rather than a currently running query, holds the resource W needs.',
        'The operator sends pg_cancel_backend(H). A true return says the signal was sent; H has no active query to cancel.',
        'Resampling still finds H idle in transaction, its table lock granted and W waiting. The dependency remains.',
        'No history result has arrived. H’s transaction still needs deliberate completion by its owner, or a separate decision to end the session.'
      ],
      'cancel-waiter': [
        'W is the active statement, but H owns the conflicting lock. Cancelling the visible waiter and releasing its blocker are different actions.',
        'The operator sends pg_cancel_backend(W), after checking W’s current identity and statement.',
        'W receives query_canceled. H still holds ACCESS EXCLUSIVE. If W used BEGIN, its transaction is now failed.',
        'W rolls back before its client is returned. H still blocks a fresh history attempt; fewer waiters alone does not establish recovery.'
      ],
      terminate: [
        'H is the known lock-only transaction. Terminating a session with business work would require a different loss decision.',
        'The operator requests pg_terminate_backend(H, 1000). This gives the function a bounded wait for session termination.',
        'Termination is observed: H is gone and its transaction’s lock has been released. W can proceed.',
        'W returns 103 then 101. H’s disconnected client must be discarded; check service recovery without releasing a wave of reconnects.'
      ]
    };
    const player = stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:step=>{
      const action = choose.value;
      const row = [...base];
      const released = step >= 2 && (action === 'rollback' || action === 'terminate');
      if(released) {
        row[0]=action==='terminate'?'Session ended':'Idle · transaction ended';
        row[1]=action==='terminate'?'H’s client disconnected':'ROLLBACK completed';
        row[2]='H’s lock released'; row[3]='W can acquire ACCESS SHARE';
        row[4]=step===3?'Rows consumed':'Read completes';row[5]='103 · pending, then 101 · paid';row[6]='H released';row[7]='W proceeds';
      }
      if(step>=2 && action==='cancel-waiter') {row[4]='Statement cancelled';row[5]=step===3?'ROLLBACK completed before reuse':'Explicit transaction failed';row[7]='W stopped';}
      fields.forEach((key,i)=>{root.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`).textContent=row[i];});
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=stories[action][step];
      root.setAttribute('data-released',String(released));
      root.setAttribute('data-stopped',String(step>=2 && action==='cancel-waiter'));
    }});
    choose.addEventListener('change',()=>{root.querySelector('[data-reset]').click();player.render();});
  });
</script>
